---
import BaseLayout from "../../site/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import "../../site/styles/eyebrow-study.css";
---

<BaseLayout title="Section label study — Mourne Made" description="A visual study of section labels for Mourne Made." hideFooter>
  <main class="eyebrow-study">
    <div class="shell eyebrow-study-intro">
      <a class="eyebrow-study-back" href="/prototypes/tag-study/">← Tag study</a>
      <p class="home-kicker">Mourne Made · component study</p>
      <h1>How should a section begin?</h1>
      <p class="eyebrow-study-lede">Three ways to introduce a section without competing with the heading beneath it.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="shell eyebrow-study-grid">
      <article class="eyebrow-option"><p class="eyebrow-option-name"><span>A</span> Yellow mark</p><div class="eyebrow-demo eyebrow-demo--mark">Rooted here</div><p>The current treatment: a short yellow bar adds a clear brand cue and a little energy.</p></article>
      <article class="eyebrow-option"><p class="eyebrow-option-name"><span>B</span> Rule label</p><div class="eyebrow-demo eyebrow-demo--rule">Rooted here</div><p>A full-width rule creates a firmer editorial break while keeping the label compact.</p></article>
      <article class="eyebrow-option"><p class="eyebrow-option-name"><span>C</span> Plain label</p><div class="eyebrow-demo eyebrow-demo--plain">Rooted here</div><p>Most restrained. Weight and colour are enough when the surrounding layout is doing more work.</p></article>
    </div>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
